name On Foundations, Walls, and the Weight of Hope
msg
On Foundations, Walls, and the Weight of Hope
by Veyrix Scale-Eyed

Scorn was founded in 435 EK by Skud, whose tent became a city and whose name became empire. From that first claim upon the Great Continent rose the western seat of Imperial power, guarded by the Great Tower of Watch and, later, by the Great Wall itself. Dragons had ruled these lands long before men arrived, yet the Empire pushed them beyond the mountains and named the exile ?peace.? For four centuries this lie held, until ambition cracked it.

Enteranni the Red believed history could be staged. By unleashing the dragons, he sought to crown himself savior. Instead, Scorn was broken beneath falling stone, its people fleeing into marsh and shadow. Only Azuriner the Careful prevailed, wielding the Golden Lance of Lythander?said by Mandor the Mad to command the skies themselves. He rebuilt Scorn not beside its corpse, but atop it, sealing the Old City as ?the domain of the past.? Power prefers burial to confession.

Azuriner?s tomb, if the old accounts are true, lies below with the Lance, the doors sealed and the deeper key sent back across the High Ocean to Khelens. No ship has crossed those waters since the Flame Wars. Perhaps that is mercy.

The heavens themselves bear witness to these cycles. Ranisha, Asferenn, and Wolfen?Snarfa, Skorta, and Svertzika?circle Bigworld endlessly, indifferent to empires that rise and fall beneath their light.

Brittany tells the same story in another voice. The Last Men fled there to escape the werebeasts born of a mage?s unpaid bargain. Mountains were raised, time was locked, and survival was purchased at the cost of isolation. Unbeknownst to them, the Five Ones slew the werebeasts long ago. Brittany endured alone, believing itself last of humanity, until light itself bridged the lie. War nearly followed. Only the return of the Five prevented another Scorn.

Hope, however, does not obey borders. Lorkas of Amudrias carried it east and west aboard the Horizon, in the form of the White Bird of Hope. He used it to heal, to fight, to endure plague and war, always believing he would return to the Golden City and to Sonja. He never did. Legends claim he vanished at sea, or sleeps beneath Old Scorn itself, hope entombed but not extinguished.

Even the gods reflect this pattern. Gnat the Cosmic Gnu, creator in Suranimite belief, was erased because creation itself was unsettling. Ada promised an end. Xathena imposed structure. And so they were burned from scripture. Yet prophecy claims that ages turn, powers fade, and even creators sleep.

Stone is laid atop stone.
endmsg
